\f1\b \cf0 Subject:
\f0\b0  Legal Review and Recommended Next Steps \'96 LLW Construction, Inc. Dispute\
\a0\

\f1\b Good afternoon Mr. Devlin and Ms. Bell,
\f0\b0 \
\a0\
I hope this message finds you well. Following our review of your documents and our recent discussion, I am providing a summary of the situation involving LLW Construction, Inc., along with legal considerations and our recommendations for moving forward.\
\a0\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \strokec3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa327\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs32\fsmilli16380 \cf0 \strokec2 1. FACTUAL SUMMARY\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs28 \cf0 \a0\
\a0Based on our review, we understand that the issues began after you engaged LLW Construction, Inc. to complete repairs to your home located at
\f1\b 3414 South Belcher Drive, Tampa, FL 33629
\f0\b0 , following damage from Hurricane Helene. The total contract amount was
\f1\b $128,355.77
\f0\b0 , of which
\f1\b $100,000 has already been paid
\f0\b0 .\
\a0\
Despite this substantial payment:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The contractor has
\f1\b not completed the project
\f0\b0 .\
\ls1\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The work performed has been
\f1\b substandard
\f0\b0 , including serious construction defects such as improper bathroom framing requiring you to reconstruct it yourself.\
\ls1\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Since January, the contractor\'92s only communications have been
\f1\b requests for more money
\f0\b0 , despite minimal progress.\
\ls1\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The contractor has stated they are
\f1\b out of funds
\f0\b0  and require additional payment to continue.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0
\cf0 Additionally, you have received a
\f1\b Notice to Owner from a subcontractor for over $3,000
\f0\b0 , indicating they were not paid by the contractor for their work.\
\a0\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \strokec3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \strokec2 \a0\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa327\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs32\fsmilli16380 \cf0 2. IMPLIED WARRANTY & CONSTRUCTION DEFECTS (Fla. Stat. Chapter 558)\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs28 \cf0 \a0\
Under Florida law, an
\f1\b implied warranty
\f0\b0  exists that all work will be performed in a competent and workmanlike manner. You may have claims under this implied warranty due to:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Defective or incomplete construction\
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Failure to meet industry standards\
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Structural and functional deficiencies\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0
\cf0 Florida Statutes, Chapter 558, requires the following steps before pursuing litigation:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls3\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 You must provide
\f1\b 60 days\'92 written notice
\f0\b0  to the contractor identifying the defects and giving them an opportunity to repair.\
\ls3\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The contractor then has
\f1\b 45 days to respond
\f0\b0  with a proposed repair plan and timeline.\
\ls3\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 You
\f1\b cannot file suit
\f0\b0  without completing this statutory notice-and-opportunity-to-repair process.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \strokec3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \strokec2 \a0\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa327\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs32\fsmilli16380 \cf0 3. BREACH OF CONTRACT CLAIM\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs28 \cf0 \a0\
You may also have a
\f1\b breach of contract claim
\f0\b0 . To prevail, you must show:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls4\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	1	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 A
\f1\b valid contract
\f0\b0  exists (which it does),\
\ls4\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	2	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 A
\f1\b material breach
\f0\b0  occurred (e.g., failure to complete or properly perform the work),\
\ls4\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	3	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 You have sustained
\f1\b damages
\f0\b0  as a result.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0
\cf0 The contractor\'92s failure to perform as agreed, including leaving work unfinished and failing to meet specifications, supports a potential cause of action for breach of contract. You may be entitled to:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls5\ilvl0
\f1\b \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Monetary damages
\f0\b0 \
\ls5\ilvl0
\f1\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Cost of hiring a replacement contractor
\f0\b0 \
\ls5\ilvl0
\f1\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Reimbursement for subcontractor payments
\f0\b0 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls5\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Other remedies under the contract and Florida law\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \strokec3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \strokec2 \a0\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa327\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs32\fsmilli16380 \cf0 4. LIENS AND NOTICE TO OWNER (Fla. Stat. \'a7 713.02 and \'a7 713.06)\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs28 \cf0 \a0\
Subcontractors who have not been paid have the right to file a
\f1\b mechanic\'92s lien
\f0\b0  against your property:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls6\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The
\f1\b Notice to Owner
\f0\b0  you received is a statutory prerequisite to filing such a lien.\
\ls6\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 If not resolved, the subcontractor may proceed to
\f1\b record a lien
\f0\b0 , which can cloud title to your property and create additional legal exposure.\
\ls6\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Even if you have already paid the general contractor,
\f1\b Florida law may still hold you liable
\f0\b0  for unpaid amounts to subcontractors.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \a0\
You may need to
\f1\b pay the subcontractor directly
\f0\b0  to avoid a lien and then
\f1\b seek reimbursement
\f0\b0  from LLW Construction.\
\a0\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \strokec3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \strokec2 \a0\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa327\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs32\fsmilli16380 \cf0 5. RECOMMENDED NEXT STEPS\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs28 \cf0 \a0\
We recommend the following course of action:\
\a0\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf0 A. Issue a Letter of Representation and Demand Letter:
\f0\b0 \
Our firm can send a
\f1\b formal letter of representation
\f0\b0  and
\f1\b demand letter
\f0\b0  to LLW Construction on your behalf. This letter will:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls7\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Demand that the contractor complete the project as agreed;\
\ls7\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Provide formal notice under Chapter 558;\
\ls7\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Seek reimbursement for payments you\'92ve made or will make to subcontractors;\
\ls7\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Initiate a resolution process that may avoid litigation and protect your property rights.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \a0\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf0 B. Pay the Subcontractor to Avoid a Lien (and Potential Foreclosure Risk):
\f0\b0 \
\a0\
You have received a
\f1\b Notice to Owner
\f0\b0  from a subcontractor who has not been paid by LLW Construction. This notice is the
\f1\b first step toward filing a construction lien
\f0\b0  against your property. In Florida, once a lien is recorded, the subcontractor may initiate a
\f1\b foreclosure action
\f0\b0  to enforce the lien and recover the amount owed. While this is not always immediate, the risk should not be taken lightly\'97
\f1\b foreclosure of a construction lien can ultimately lead to the forced sale of your home
\f0\b0  if not resolved.\
\a0\
To protect your property interest and avoid this outcome, we recommend that you
\f1\b consider paying the subcontractor directly
\f0\b0  the amount owed\'97approximately
\f1\b $3,000+
\f0\b0 \'97to satisfy the underlying debt. This action would:\
\a0\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls8\ilvl0
\f1\b \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Prevent the recording of a lien
\f0\b0  or facilitate its removal if already recorded;\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls8\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Avoid legal fees, interest, and costs that would accrue if the subcontractor proceeds with litigation;\
\ls8\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Protect your property title from encumbrances, which could impact your ability to refinance or sell;\
\ls8\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Allow you to maintain control over the dispute and avoid being caught in the middle of a payment conflict between the contractor and subcontractor.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \a0\
If you proceed with payment, we strongly advise:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls9\ilvl0
\f1\b \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Obtaining a written release of lien or lien waiver
\f0\b0  from the subcontractor;\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls9\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Retaining proof of payment (cancelled check, receipt, signed acknowledgment);\
\ls9\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Using this payment as part of your damages claim in pursuing
\f1\b reimbursement from LLW Construction
\f0\b0 , who failed in their contractual obligation to pay their vendors.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0
\cf0 This proactive step helps mitigate your risk and strengthens your position in any forthcoming demand or legal action against the contractor.\
\a0\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf0 C. Schedule a Call:
\f0\b0 \
Please let us know if you would like us to proceed with drafting and sending the above-referenced letters. We would also be happy to schedule a call to discuss any questions you may have.\
\a0\
Thank you, and we remain committed to protecting your interests throughout this process.\
\a0\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
